System.out.println("You enter a room with a door to the left and a door to the right.");
System.out.println("1. Go left.");
System.out.println("2. Go right.");

Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
String choice = scanner.nextLine();

if (choice.equals("1")) {
    // go left
} else if (choice.equals("2")) {
    // go right
} else {
    System.out.println("Invalid choice.");
}
But if you want to make it more robust, you can loop until the user enters a valid choice.
